Images
- The VS Code icon (film/public/brand/vscode.svg), Microsoft: used whole and unaltered, as the brand guidelines ask
  (code.visualstudio.com/brand).
- The merge icon in film/src/kit/Ground.tsx: Fluent UI System Icons, Microsoft, MIT.
- film/public/scenes/lighthouse-*.png: example images for the list-actions scene, generated for this film.
- film/public/fx/grain-*.png: film grain tiles, generated for this film.
- Every app, page, desktop and icon the scenes draw is an original drawing; there are no third-party logos.

Sound
- film/assets/music/theme.flac: an original instrumental made for this film with ACE-Step
  (film/assets/music/theme.json has its prompt and seeds).
- film/public/sfx/*.wav: sound effects synthesized for this film.

Example (skills/generate-changelog-film/example/2026-10-19)
- The recordings are of VS Code Insiders; the narration is MAI-Voice-2 (Azure AI Speech).

Software
- Remotion (remotion.dev): the film renders with Remotion, which is free for individuals and small teams and needs a
  company licence otherwise (remotion.dev/license).
- The changelog-videos plugin (vscode-team-kit, MIT): its engine makes the projects, recordings and narration; this
  repo's setup copies and patches it locally and never changes the plugin.
